{"id":12263,"date":"2026-07-13T05:47:45","date_gmt":"2026-07-13T05:47:45","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/?page_id=12263"},"modified":"2026-07-23T04:40:49","modified_gmt":"2026-07-23T04:40:49","slug":"activities-of-rd-cell","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/college-research-cell\/activities-of-rd-cell\/","title":{"rendered":"Activities of R&#038;D Cell"},"content":{"rendered":"<p><strong><u>Activities of R&amp;D Cell<\/u><\/strong><\/p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>JASETM: <\/strong>Journal of Applied Science, Engineering, Technology and Management (JASETM) is a half-yearly online journal published in-house by FISAT.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Webinar on Research Publication: <\/strong>The Research &amp; Development (R&amp;D) cell at FISAT has organized a webinar on \u201cResearch Publication and Journal Indexing\u201d on 28th September 2023. Resource person: Dr. Elammaran Jayamani, Associate Professor, Swinburne University of Technology Sarawak Campus (SUTS). Around 30 faculty members and research scholars from various departments attended the webinar.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Amrit Kaal Vimarsh: Viksit Bharat@2047:<\/strong> The Research &amp; Development (R&amp;D) cell at FISAT has organized an invited talk titled <strong>\u201cRole of Academia in Defense R&amp;D eco system\u201d<\/strong> on 23<sup>rd<\/sup> February 2024. Resource person: Dr. Ajith Kumar K, Director, Naval Physical &amp; Oceanographic Laboratory (NPOL), DRDO. Around 240 Students and faculty members from various departments attended the session.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Invited Talk titled Essence of Research in Academe: <\/strong>The Research &amp; Development (R&amp;D) cell at FISAT has organized an invited talk titled \u201c<strong>Essence of Research in Academe<\/strong>\u201d on 14<sup>th<\/sup> March 2024. Resource person: Dr. Raman Unnikrishnan, Professor, College of Engineering and Computer Science, California State University, Fullerton, California, USA. Around 50 faculty members and research scholars from various departments attended the session.<\/li>\n<li><strong>A technical session on Research Methodology<\/strong> was organized on 24-01-2025. The resource person was Dr. R Sridharan, Professor, NIT Calicut. Around 50 faculty members and research scholars from various departments attended the session.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p><strong>Project competitions and exhibitions<\/strong><\/p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Women Hackathon 3.0: <\/strong>FISAT Technology Business Incubator (TBI) and Research &amp; Development (R&amp;D) cell, in collaboration with the Ministry of Micro, Small &amp; Medium Enterprises (MSME) Gov. of India, organized the Women Hackathon 3.0 in August 2023. This event provided a platform for women-led teams to showcase their innovative ideas and an opportunity for incubation with funding. Six teams participated in the event and 4 ideas were shortlisted and recommended to MSME for funding.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Rural Innovators Meet (RIM) organized by KSCSTE: <\/strong>Rural Innovators Meet (RIM) is a programme for encouraging and promoting the unorganized rural and grass root innovators engaged in the development of rural technologies.<\/li>\n<li><strong>VSSC World Space Week 2023: <\/strong>Vikram Sarabhai Space Centre (VSSC), Liquid Propulsion Systems Centre (LPSC), ISRO Inertial Systems Unit (IISU) &amp; Indian Institute of Space Science &amp; Technology (IIST) under Indian Space Research Organization (ISRO) conducted a one-day workshop on 5<sup>th<\/sup> October 2023 in Trivandrum with the theme &#8220;Space and Entrepreneurship&#8221;. The workshop offered an opportunity for our students to pitch their ideas in space sector.<\/li>\n<li>7 women faculty &amp; IEDC staff in charge attended the \u201c<strong>Women in STEM are vital to Future Development<\/strong>&#8221; programme from FISAT organized by Kerala Startup Mission in collaboration with the British High Commission in India, Chevening alumni, and the University of Oxford.<\/li>\n<li><strong>KETCON 2024<\/strong> &#8211; APJ AKTU TECHFEST: 3 student teams from FISAT have participated and won accolades at the TECHFEST organized by APJ Abdul Kalam Technological University, Thiruvananthapuram and hosted at Ahalia School of Engineering and Technology, Palakkad.<\/li>\n<li><strong>AICTE Millets Recipe Unleashing Talent (AMRUT): <\/strong>AMRUT is a Millet recipe preparation competition for students, serving faculties and supporting staff from approved institutions to and come out with innovative yet traditional recipes. Two teams from FISAT submitted the application for AICTE Millets Recipe Unleashing Talent (AMRUT)<\/li>\n<li><strong>AICTE VAANI (Vibrant Advocacy for advancement and Nurturing of Indian Languages): <\/strong>Two faculty attended the webinar on the launch of VAANI scheme. It was decided to apply for the VAANI scheme and we received a funding assistance offer for 2 lakh rupees to organise the seminar.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p><strong>\u00a0<\/strong><strong><u>IPR Cell &#8211; Intellectual Property of FISAT<\/u><\/strong><\/p>\n<p>The Intellectual Property Rights (IPR) Cell at FISAT is set up under the R&amp;D Cell with an aim to foster and endorse original ideas, designs or creations by inculcating innovation and creativity among the faculty and students of the institution. FISAT has instituted a variety of schemes and policies designed to bolster and facilitate the filing and publication of patent-worthy concepts.<\/p>\n<p>The IPR Cell at FISAT organises regular awareness programmes and events to familiarise the concept of intellectual property and the need for protecting it through patents and copyrights. IPR Cell extends comprehensive assistance to faculty members and students in the process of patent application\/filing and publishing of patentable ideas and also continuously monitors the process until the patent gets granted. Financial support is also allocated exclusively to published patents\/intellectual property, under the stipulation that the Federal Institute of Science and Technology (FISAT) is a co-applicant in the application.<\/p>\n<p><strong><u>Activities of IPR Cell<\/u><\/strong><\/p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>IPR awareness programme: Understanding Intellectual Property Rights (IPR): An Asset to Engineers: <\/strong>An IPR awareness programme titled \u201cUnderstanding Intellectual Property Rights (IPR): An Asset to Engineers\u201d was organised by the IPR CELL at FISAT in association with DPIIT-IPR Chair &amp; Inter University Centre for IPR Studies (IUCIPRS) at Cochin University of Science and Technology (CUSAT), Cochin. The programme was conducted on 24th Nov 2023 from 1:30 PM to 4:00 PM at Conference Hall (AB 205) of FISAT. The target audience included the students and staff of FISAT. A total of 62 participants attended the sessions.\u00a0 The sessions emphasized on the role of IPRs in the journey of an engineering graduate. <strong>Resource Persons: <\/strong><strong>Dr. M. Bhasi, <\/strong>Director, IUCIPRS, CUSAT &amp; Co-Ordinator, DPIIT-IPR Chair, <strong>Mr. Muhammed Faris V <\/strong>Research Assistant DPIIT-IPR Chair, IUCIPRS, CUSAT<\/li>\n<li><strong>Workshop on IPR studies:<\/strong> IPR Cell FISAT organized a One-day workshop on \u201cPatents and Copyright Filing Procedures in India\u201d on 18th August 2023. Resource person: Prof. J E Moshe Dayan (Coordinator, PSNA IPR Cell, PSNA CET, Dindigul). He has extensive knowledge and experience in the field of Intellectual Property Rights. 32 faculty members from various departments attended the workshop.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Activities of R&amp;D Cell JASETM: Journal of Applied Science, Engineering, Technology and Management (JASETM) is a half-yearly online journal published in-house by FISAT. Webinar on Research Publication: The Research &amp; Development (R&amp;D) cell at FISAT has organized a webinar on \u201cResearch Publication and Journal Indexing\u201d on 28th September 2023. Resource person: Dr. Elammaran Jayamani, Associate [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":87,"featured_media":0,"parent":360,"menu_order":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","template":"research.php","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"footnotes":""},"class_list":["post-12263","page","type-page","status-publish","hentry"],"acf":[],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/12263","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/page"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/87"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=12263"}],"version-history":[{"count":3,"href":"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/12263\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":12531,"href":"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/12263\/revisions\/12531"}],"up":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/360"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/fisat.ac.in\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=12263"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}